From dcc3fce05c5c83fd56a51bde362805b8ffdac100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:24:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: platform: Add QuickLogic CSSP camera interface driver

Add a media controller driver for the QuickLogic CSSP bridge on the TI
GPMC bus, used on the BeagleBone camera capes. The bridge has one mode
register, a pixel data port and no interrupt; the frame size is the DMA
length.

The driver exposes a bridge subdevice and a capture video node with
MC-centric formats, owns the cape power rails and reset, and links the
sensor to itself so the rails stay on while the sensor is in use. Data is
moved by one cyclic dmaengine transfer into a ring of frame-sized bounce
buffers and copied into vb2 buffers from a work item, which keeps the
stream gap-free on the stock EDMA driver. Each DMA request reads the
fixed-address data port (AB-synchronised, one word per element), which
any slave DMA engine can do. A watchdog and recovery path restarts a
stalled or misaligned stream, and frames around a misaligned period are
completed with an error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
